From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rui Figueira <rfigueira@cloudflare.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 19:23:24 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Apply ancestor overflow clips to hoisted z-index children
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A positioned box with a z-index paints with its stacking context, not
with its parent. That skipped the overflow clip of every box between
the two, so content that sits inside an `overflow: hidden` box in
Chrome painted outside it. A collapsed disclosure panel (height 0,
overflow hidden) leaked its z-indexed children: radar.cloudflare.com's
sidebar showed the guide line of every closed submenu.

Each hoisted child now paints inside the intersection of the clips on
its layout-parent chain up to the stacking context. That chain runs
through an abspos box's containing block, so a clip outside the
containing block still does not apply. Nothing on the chain has a
transform, because a transform would make that box the stacking
context.

beep-boop-🤖
